-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhfwhi75", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Eu não falo português.", "en": "I don't speak Portuguese.", "ex": "", "tags": ["introductions", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhfiayoh", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Você poderia repetir?", "en": "Could you repeat?", "ex": "", "tags": ["introductions", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhfkcfwf", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Eu não entendi.", "en": "I didn't understand.", "ex": "", "tags": ["introductions", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhfyvmor", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Tudo certo?", "en": "How's everything?", "ex": "", "tags": ["politeness", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhfn35j2", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Até mais tarde.", "en": "See you later.", "ex": "", "tags": ["politeness", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhfhxqoq", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Entre, por favor.", "en": "Come in, please.", "ex": "", "tags": ["politeness", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhfmfwoe", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Muito obrigado.", "en": "Thank you very much. (fml./m.)", "ex": "", "tags": ["politeness", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhfav06v", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Muito obrigada.", "en": "Thank you very much. (fml./f.)", "ex": "", "tags": ["politeness", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhfkpmfj", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Não há de que.", "en": "Don't mention it.", "ex": "", "tags": ["politeness", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhf03xj4", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Faça o favor.", "en": "Please (infml.)", "ex": "Abra a janela, faça o favor. — Open the window, will you?", "tags": ["politeness", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhgozk9j", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Faça-me um favor.", "en": "Do me a favor.", "ex": "", "tags": ["politeness", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhg33l81", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Você pode me ajudar?", "en": "Can you help me?", "ex": "", "tags": ["politeness", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhgas3gv", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "O senhor poderia me ajudar?", "en": "Could you help me? (fml./m.)", "ex": "", "tags": ["politeness", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhg3o0h7", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "A senhora poderia me ajudar?", "en": "Could you help me? (fml./f.)", "ex": "", "tags": ["politeness", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhgrooj6", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Socorro!", "en": "Help! (in an emergency)", "ex": "", "tags": ["politeness", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhg9hy05", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Esta é …", "en": "This is … (introducing someone)", "ex": "Esta é a Jane.", "tags": ["dialogue", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhgxyz05", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Você é americana?", "en": "Are you American? (to a woman)", "ex": "", "tags": ["dialogue", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhg4t40c", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Eu sou australiana.", "en": "I'm Australian. (woman speaking)", "ex": "Não, eu sou australiana.", "tags": ["dialogue", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhg1qeyl", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Bem-vindo/a ao Brasil!", "en": "Welcome to Brazil! (m./f.)", "ex": "Bem-vinda ao Brasil!", "tags": ["dialogue", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhgm4ww7", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Legal!", "en": "Cool!", "ex": "", "tags": ["dialogue", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhg6tciy", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Eu falo um pouco de português.", "en": "I speak a little Portuguese.", "ex": "", "tags": ["classroom", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhgej1aw", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Estou aprendendo português.", "en": "I'm learning Portuguese.", "ex": "", "tags": ["classroom", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhg3adi2", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Fale mais devagar.", "en": "Speak more slowly.", "ex": "", "tags": ["classroom", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhg0fw5i", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Parabéns!", "en": "Congratulations!", "ex": "", "tags": ["classroom", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}, {"id": "mtdbrkhg3pwfa", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "pt": "Muito bem!", "en": "Very good!", "ex": "", "tags": ["classroom", "lesson 1"], "box": 0, "reviews": 0, "right": 0, "lapses": 0, "created": "2026-08-28", "audio": null}], "notes": [{"id": "mtdbrkhg920f3", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "title": "Lesson goals", "body": "", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "text": "Bem-vindos! This lesson covers the basic expressions and the handful of words and phrases you need to start speaking Portuguese at all."}, {"t": "h", "text": "By the end you should be able to"}, {"t": "list", "items": ["greet people at different times of the day  ·  p. 10", "address someone formally and informally  ·  p. 12", "introduce yourself and say your name  ·  p. 13", "ask other people's names and find out how they're doing  ·  p. 16", "put it all together in a simple conversation  ·  p. 19"]}, {"t": "h", "text": "Abbreviations used throughout the course"}, {"t": "table", "head": ["Short", "Means"], "rows": [["(m.)", "masculine"], ["(f.)", "feminine"], ["(sg.)", "singular"], ["(pl.)", "plural"], ["(fml.)", "formal"], ["(infml.)", "informal"], ["(lit.)", "literally"]]}, {"t": "h", "text": "Audio tracks — CD 1"}, {"t": "table", "head": ["Section", "Track"], "rows": [["1A Vocabulary Builder 1", "2"], ["1B Take It Further", "3"], ["1C Grammar Builder 1", "4"], ["1D Vocabulary Builder 2", "5"], ["1E Take It Further", "6"], ["1F Grammar Builder 2", "7"], ["1G Bring It All Together", "8"], ["1H Take It Further", "9"]]}], "source": "p. 9", "date": "2026-08-28", "read": false}, {"id": "mtdbrkhgh668m", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "title": "Pronunciation — accents and special symbols", "body": "", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "text": "Portuguese uses a handful of orthographic marks. Each one does a specific job — three change the sound, one changes nothing at all."}, {"t": "table", "head": ["Accent", "What it does", "Example", "Sound in English"], "rows": [["~ til", "makes the vowel nasal", "não (no)", "like the ou in bound"], ["", "", "aviões (airplanes)", "like the o in don't, then the e in get"], ["", "", "mãe (mother)", "like the u in thunder, then the e in get"], ["´ agudo", "marks the stressed syllable; on e and o it also opens the vowel", "café (coffee)", "like the e in best"], ["", "", "nós (we)", "like the o in off (northeastern U.S.)"], ["", "", "possível (possible)", "like the i in routine"], ["^ circunflexo", "the vowel is stressed and closed", "você (you)", "like the ay in day, clipped"], ["", "", "avô (grandfather)", "like the o in go, clipped"], ["` grave", "distinguishes grammar only", "a (the) / à (to the)", "no change in sound"], ["¸ cedilha", "on c before a, o, u to give it an s sound", "açúcar (sugar)", "like the s in see"]]}, {"t": "callout", "text": "In açúcar, notice the second c is not softened — it sounds like the k in kite."}], "source": "pp. 11–12 · 1B Take It Further", "date": "2026-08-28", "read": false}, {"id": "mtdbrkhg0tkbv", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "title": "Pronunciation — M and N", "body": "", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "text": "At the end of a word, or in the middle before a consonant, m and n nasalize the vowel in front of them and aren't really pronounced on their own."}, {"t": "pairs", "rows": [["ponte (bridge)", "the n makes the o nasal, like the on in don't"], ["cama (bed)", "the first a is nasal like the un in bunch; the second is not — it's the a in father"], ["bom (good)", "a word-final m is pronounced as an n; om sounds like on in don't"]]}, {"t": "h", "text": "The exception worth memorising"}, {"t": "p", "text": "An m or n sitting between two vowels forms a syllable with the second one, so the first vowel is not nasalized. In each pair below the first word is nasal and the second isn't:"}, {"t": "pairs", "rows": [["limpa (clean)", "lima (lime)"], ["grande (big)", "grana (money, infml.)"]]}, {"t": "callout", "text": "At the start of a word they behave like English: mala (suitcase) has the m of Mary, nada (nothing) the n of nest."}], "source": "pp. 15–16 · 1E Take It Further", "date": "2026-08-28", "read": false}, {"id": "mtdbrkhg7wln9", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "title": "Greetings — formal and informal", "body": "", "blocks": [{"t": "h", "text": "Why obrigado has two endings"}, {"t": "p", "text": "Portuguese nouns and adjectives carry gender, and obrigado/a agrees with the person speaking — not the person being thanked. A woman says obrigada; a man says obrigado."}, {"t": "h", "text": "Choosing how to address someone"}, {"t": "p", "text": "você works for men and women alike and is the informal default — family, friends, anyone your own age. To be formal, swap você for o senhor or a senhora, matching the gender of the person you're speaking to."}, {"t": "table", "head": ["", "Informal", "Formal (m.)", "Formal (f.)"], "rows": [["How are you?", "Como vai você?", "Como vai o senhor?", "Como vai a senhora?"], ["I'm fine, and you?", "Tudo bem, e você?", "Estou bem, e o senhor?", "Estou bem, e a senhora?"]]}, {"t": "h", "text": "Senhor and senhora with names"}, {"t": "p", "text": "Before a last name they work like Mr. and Mrs./Ms., and read as the highest level of formality in Brazil. Written short: Sr. and Sra. With a first name it's also common — Senhor shortens to Seu (Seu Agenor), and Senhora can become Dona (Dona Maria)."}, {"t": "pairs", "rows": [["Você fala português, Paulo?", "informal"], ["O senhor fala português, Sr. Paulo?", "formal"], ["O senhor fala português, Sr. Smith?", "very formal"]]}, {"t": "h", "text": "Two pairs not to mix up"}, {"t": "callout", "text": "Você pode me ajudar? asks a favour. Socorro! is for an emergency — don't reach for it when you mean the first.\n\nFaça-me um favor. asks a favour too. Faça o favor. is an informal softener on a request: Abra a janela, faça o favor. — Open the window, will you?"}], "source": "pp. 12–13, 16–17 · Grammar Builders 1 & 2", "date": "2026-08-28", "read": false}, {"id": "mtdbrkhg16hp5", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "title": "The dialogue — Sandra, Gustavo and Jane", "body": "", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "text": "An informal three-way introduction. Sandra runs into Gustavo and opens with Oi and E aí?; he answers Tudo bem. She introduces her friend with Esta é a Jane, and Gustavo and Jane exchange Prazer. Gustavo asks Você é americana? — Jane answers Não, eu sou australiana — and he welcomes her with Bem-vinda ao Brasil! Jane closes with Legal!"}, {"t": "h", "text": "Structures to notice"}, {"t": "list", "items": ["Esta é … introduces a third person", "Prazer works as a two-way exchange — both people say it", "nationality adjectives agree with the speaker: americana, australiana are the feminine forms", "bem-vindo / bem-vinda agrees with the person being welcomed"]}, {"t": "h", "text": "The same conversation, formally"}, {"t": "p", "text": "Work Out 2 on p. 20 rewrites it with Sra. Dias, Sr. Morais and Sr. Smith: Como vai o senhor? / Estou bem / Quero lhe apresentar / Muito prazer / O prazer é meu / O senhor é americano? / Não / Bem-vindo / Muito obrigado. Same conversation, every register lifted."}], "source": "p. 19 · 1G Bring It All Together, CD 1 track 8", "date": "2026-08-28", "read": false}, {"id": "mtdbrkhg9reyd", "chapterId": "mtdbrkhf2s2ai", "title": "Practice — say it out loud", "body": "", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "text": "Answer each one before you reveal it. There's often more than one right answer."}, {"t": "h", "text": "Drive It Home — p. 21"}, {"t": "ex", "items": [{"q": "Greet a friend in the morning and ask if everything is fine.", "a": "Bom dia, tudo bem?"}, {"q": "Greet an elderly neighbour in the evening and ask how she is.", "a": "Boa noite, como vai a senhora?"}, {"q": "Introduce Rita, a colleague, to Mr. Silva, and tell her Mr. Silva is Brazilian.", "a": "Sr. Silva, quero lhe apresentar Rita. Rita, Sr. Silva é brasileiro."}, {"q": "Introduce Antônio, a friend, to another friend, Sandra.", "a": "Antônio, gostaria de lhe apresentar Sandra."}, {"q": "Greet an elderly woman in the afternoon and ask her name.", "a": "Boa tarde. Como a senhora se chama?"}, {"q": "Say thank you and good-bye to a salesman at a shop.", "a": "Muito obrigado / muito obrigada. Até logo."}, {"q": "Apologize, say you didn't understand, then ask a gentleman to repeat.", "a": "Desculpe, eu não entendi. O senhor poderia repetir?"}, {"q": "Say excuse me, ask a stranger if she speaks English, then say you don't speak Portuguese.", "a": "Com licença, a senhora fala inglês? Eu não falo português."}]}, {"t": "h", "text": "Word Recall — p. 23"}, {"t": "ex", "intro": "How would you answer each of these?", "items": [{"q": "Obrigada.", "a": "De nada."}, {"q": "Você é brasileiro?", "a": "Não, eu sou …"}, {"q": "Como vai?", "a": "Tudo bem."}, {"q": "Até logo.", "a": "Até logo."}, {"q": "Você fala português?", "a": "Sim, eu falo um pouco de português. / Sim, estou aprendendo português."}, {"q": "Gostaria de lhe apresentar a Sra. Medeiros.", "a": "Muito prazer, Sra. Medeiros."}, {"q": "Como você se chama?", "a": "Eu me chamo …"}, {"q": "Parabéns!", "a": "Obrigado / obrigada."}]}], "source": "pp. 21, 23 · Drive It Home and Word Recall", "date": "2026-08-28", "read": false}], "sessions": []}